{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_015 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the best performer so far at 0.6287 accuracy with very low cost (4.54 GPU hrs), slightly beating config_009 (resnet50, concat) at 0.6186. Image-only is clearly inferior (0.3275), confirming multimodal is essential. Question: config_005 is the direct extension of config_015 with only the fusion strategy changed from concat to weighted. This tests whether learning a weighted combination of modalities (rather than simple concatenation) can further improve accuracy, which is a fundamental design choice in multimodal fusion. Rationale: This is the cheapest and most interpretable next step—same architecture, same encoders, same aggregation—so any accuracy difference is attributable to the fusion mechanism. Expected cost is similar to config_015 (~4-5 GPU hrs), making it very affordable. If weighted fusion helps, it establishes a direction for combining with other improvements (e.g., transformer aggregation, different RNA encoders) in subsequent experiments. If it does not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can pivot to testing RNA encoder or aggregation changes with the remaining budget."
}

